# mikrotik6 Phase 2 -- secrets for the other mikrotik6-p2-*.rsc scripts.
# rb5009-migration.md Phase 2.
#
# TEMPLATE ONLY. Never put real values in this file: it is in git.
# Copy it to home/network/backups/mikrotik6-p2-secrets.rsc (gitignored),
# fill the values from mikrotik1's "/export show-sensitive" (Phase 0), then:
#   scp backups/mikrotik6-p2-secrets.rsc admin@router6.home.ledcom.fr:
#   /import mikrotik6-p2-secrets.rsc
#   /file/remove mikrotik6-p2-secrets.rsc
#
# The values live as globals only until the Phase 2 scripts have run.
# Remove them after:
#   /system/script/environment/remove [find where name~"^m6"]
#
# Where each value comes from in the show-sensitive export:
#   m6WgPrivateKey   /interface wireguard ... name=wireguard1 private-key="..."
#   m6CapsPass       /caps-man configuration ... name=caps_config security.passphrase=...
#                    (caps_ch11 must have the same one: both are SSID LEDCOM.
#                    If they differ, stop and tell the next session.)
#   m6CapsPassIot    /caps-man configuration ... name=caps_iot security.passphrase=...
#   m6HaPassword     not exported (user passwords never are). The password that
#                    Home Assistant's MikroTik integration uses for "homeassistant".

:global m6WgPrivateKey "REPLACE-ME"
:global m6CapsPass "REPLACE-ME"
:global m6CapsPassIot "REPLACE-ME"
:global m6HaPassword "REPLACE-ME"
